Two names cxx1 emits and cl does not, and no name that differs: `??_DD1@@QEAAXXZ` and `??_DD2@@QEAAXXZ`, the vbase destructors of the two middle classes. That is the wrapper this ABI destroys a *complete* object through - it runs `??1` and then the virtual bases, which is Itanium's D1 under a Microsoft name - and this case never destroys a D1 or a D2 as a complete object, so cl emits neither. cxx1 emits one beside every destructor of a class with a virtual base, the way it emits D1 beside every D2, and an unused COMDAT definition costs a fold. **Everything this round is about agrees with cl by name**: `??_8Dia@@7BD1@@@`, `??_8Dia@@7BD2@@@`, `??_8D1@@7B@`, `??_8D2@@7B@`, `??_DDia@@QEAAXXZ`, and the constructors that carry the hidden most-derived flag - which is not in a mangled name at all, so what the flag *does* is checked by run.sh and by this case's output on the box rather than here.
